{%- comment -%}
  Explainer figure: slope chart of six backbones' macro-F1 on VNAT, ungrouped
  vs capture-grouped split (T=3 s, 20 ms windows, eight features). Values from
  Table "leakage" of the accepted CCNC 2027 paper (Hajaj, Meshleb, Dvir).
  y = 20 + (96 - F1) * 13 (viewBox units); labels nudged apart by at least 13.
{%- endcomment -%}
<figure class="note-figure" style="--c: var(--line-traffic)">
  <p class="fig-title">Same six models, two ways of splitting the data</p>
  <svg
    class="fig-svg fig-slope"
    viewBox="0 0 520 270"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="slope-t"
  >
    <title id="slope-t">
      Macro-F1 on VNAT before and after keeping each recording session on one side of the split. Informer 95.1 to 79.9, first to last. NST 91.4
      to 87.8, second to first. Autoformer 90.1 to 83.7. TimesNet 89.0 to 86.7. FEDformer 88.2 to 86.2. TimeMixer 86.7 to 83.1.
    </title>
    <text class="fig-label fig-axis-head" x="150" y="12" text-anchor="middle">sessions leak into the test</text>
    <text class="fig-label fig-axis-head" x="370" y="12" text-anchor="middle">sessions kept apart</text>
    <line class="fig-axis" x1="150" y1="20" x2="150" y2="250" />
    <line class="fig-axis" x1="370" y1="20" x2="370" y2="250" />
    <g class="fig-slope-line is-hl">
      <line x1="150" y1="31.4" x2="370" y2="229.0" />
      <circle cx="150" cy="31.4" r="4" />
      <circle cx="370" cy="229.0" r="4" />
      <text class="fig-label" x="140" y="35.4" text-anchor="end">Informer 95.1</text>
      <text class="fig-label" x="380" y="233.0">79.9 Informer</text>
    </g>
    <g class="fig-slope-line is-new">
      <line x1="150" y1="79.8" x2="370" y2="127.0" />
      <circle cx="150" cy="79.8" r="4" />
      <circle cx="370" cy="127.0" r="4" />
      <text class="fig-label" x="140" y="83.8" text-anchor="end">NST 91.4</text>
      <text class="fig-label" x="380" y="131.0">87.8 NST</text>
    </g>
    <g class="fig-slope-line">
      <line x1="150" y1="96.8" x2="370" y2="179.8" />
      <circle cx="150" cy="96.8" r="4" />
      <circle cx="370" cy="179.8" r="4" />
      <text class="fig-label" x="140" y="100.8" text-anchor="end">Autoformer 90.1</text>
      <text class="fig-label" x="380" y="183.8">83.7 Autoformer</text>
    </g>
    <g class="fig-slope-line">
      <line x1="150" y1="110.7" x2="370" y2="140.5" />
      <circle cx="150" cy="110.7" r="4" />
      <circle cx="370" cy="140.5" r="4" />
      <text class="fig-label" x="140" y="114.7" text-anchor="end">TimesNet 89.0</text>
      <text class="fig-label" x="380" y="144.5">86.7 TimesNet</text>
    </g>
    <g class="fig-slope-line">
      <line x1="150" y1="121.7" x2="370" y2="147.9" />
      <circle cx="150" cy="121.7" r="4" />
      <circle cx="370" cy="147.9" r="4" />
      <text class="fig-label" x="140" y="127.7" text-anchor="end">FEDformer 88.2</text>
      <text class="fig-label" x="380" y="157.5">86.2 FEDformer</text>
    </g>
    <g class="fig-slope-line">
      <line x1="150" y1="141.4" x2="370" y2="187.7" />
      <circle cx="150" cy="141.4" r="4" />
      <circle cx="370" cy="187.7" r="4" />
      <text class="fig-label" x="140" y="145.4" text-anchor="end">TimeMixer 86.7</text>
      <text class="fig-label" x="380" y="196.8">83.1 TimeMixer</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    Macro-F1 (out of 100) on the VNAT dataset. Left: the usual split, where flows from the same recording session can sit in both the training and the
    test set. Right: each session kept on one side. Informer goes from first to last and NST from second to first. From our CCNC 2027 paper.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
